Product Requirements Document (PRD)
Product Name: Agency Placement & Onboarding Hub (Free B2B SaaS)
Target Audience: Singapore Employment Agencies (EA Directors & Counter Operations Staff)
Document Owner: Product Management
Status: Draft / Initial Scope

1. Problem Statement
Singapore Employment Agencies (EAs) operating in the Foreign Domestic Worker (FDW) sector face heavy operational overhead, paper-based friction, and low profit margins per placement:
Manual Paperwork Overload: Placing a single worker requires filling out, printing, physically signing, and filing 5+ complex document sets (Standard EA Agreements, Salary Deduction Schedules, MOM IPA Letters, Safety Agreements, and House Rules). Counter staff spend 30 to 45 minutes per employer on repetitive paper signing alone.
Compliance & Chasing Bottlenecks: Post-placement administrative tracking is fragmented across paper folders and manual Excel sheets. Staff waste hours chasing employers and workers for missing documents, 6-Month Medical Exam (6ME) slips, and Work Permit renewal deadlines, creating risk of MOM regulatory fines.
Low Margin & Static Revenue Streams: Placement fees are facing downward price pressure. Agencies lack turnkey, high-margin ancillary revenue streams at the Point of Sale (POS) beyond static referral commissions from traditional insurers.

2. Expected Impact for Agencies
If Pivot C successfully solves these operational bottlenecks for Employment Agencies, the business impact will be:
70% Reduction in Counter Processing Time: Cuts employer onboarding time from ~45 minutes down to under 10 minutes via mobile e-signatures and pre-filled Singpass/MyInfo workflows.
80% Decrease in Administrative Chasing: Automated milestone tracking and cloud document storage eliminate manual follow-ups for post-placement MOM statutory deadlines.
New Zero-CapEx Revenue Stream: Agencies generate an additional S$700–S$1,000+ per month in pure profit (based on 20–30 placements/month) via the S$35 cash bounty paid on every bundled Pivot C 26-month household management package.
Zero Software Costs: Gives small-to-medium agencies enterprise-grade digital tools at S$0 cost, leveling the playing field against mega-agencies.

